# Postgres connection string (Supabase Project Settings -> Database ->
# Connection string). NOT the SUPABASE_URL/anon-key REST pair used elsewhere
# in this repo -- this is a raw Postgres DSN, needed by the ingestion
# pipeline, repositories, and the LangGraph checkpointer.
#
# Prefer the SESSION POOLER connection string (Connection Pooling -> Session
# mode), not the direct db.<ref>.supabase.co host: Supabase's direct
# connection is IPv6-only, which fails outright on networks without IPv6
# egress (Docker Desktop's default network on Windows, some VPS/CI
# environments). The session pooler is IPv4-compatible and still supports
# prepared statements (unlike the transaction-mode pooler on port 6543,
# which the LangGraph checkpointer needs prepared statements for).
# Username format changes to postgres.<project-ref> for the pooler.
SUPABASE_DB_URL=postgresql://postgres.PROJECT_REF:PASSWORD@aws-REGION.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres

GEMINI_API_KEY=your-gemini-api-key
